From: Niagara SMP investigation <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] target/sparc: preserve guest mondo across hypervisor return

The Niagara hypervisor can queue a guest mondo and raise CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD
before its vector handler executes retry.  sparc_cpu_exec_interrupt() cleared
that request before checking whether the vCPU was still in hypervisor mode, so
the guest interrupt was lost.  Under a two-CPU illumos boot this left a strand
spinning after cross-call traffic began.

Consume CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD only when QEMU takes a vector trap or is ready to
deliver the pending interrupt in guest mode.  Leave it asserted while the vCPU
finishes the hypervisor handler.
---
 target/sparc/cpu.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/sparc/cpu.c b/target/sparc/cpu.c
index d4c5388..f5eb620 100644
--- a/target/sparc/cpu.c
+++ b/target/sparc/cpu.c
@@ -95,9 +95,6 @@ static bool sparc_cpu_exec_interrupt(CPUState *cs, int interrupt_request)
 	cs->halted = 0;
 	cpu_reset_interrupt(cs, CPU_INTERRUPT_HALT);
 
-	/* clear CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD */
-        cpu_reset_interrupt(cs, CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD);
-
 	qemu_log_mask(CPU_LOG_INT,
 	"cpu:%d %s:  ivec:%lx intr_index:0x%x tl:%d pc:%lx psrpil:0x%x pil_in:%x soft:%x\n",
 		cs->cpu_index, __func__, env->ivec_status,
@@ -110,6 +107,8 @@ static bool sparc_cpu_exec_interrupt(CPUState *cs, int interrupt_request)
             && cpu_interrupts_enabled(env)
 #endif
 	) {
+            /* Consume the request before entering the vector trap. */
+            cpu_reset_interrupt(cs, CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD);
             env->interrupt_index = TT_IVEC;
             cs->exception_index = env->interrupt_index;
 
@@ -125,11 +124,16 @@ static bool sparc_cpu_exec_interrupt(CPUState *cs, int interrupt_request)
 
 	if (cpu_hypervisor_mode(env)) {
 	    /*
-	     * In hypervisor mode, only above cases are acceptable.
+	     * A hypervisor vector handler can queue a guest mondo and raise
+	     * CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD before it executes retry.  Keep that request
+	     * pending until the vCPU has returned to guest mode.
 	     */
-    	    return false;
+	    return false;
 	}
 
+        /* The request can now be consumed by a guest interrupt. */
+        cpu_reset_interrupt(cs, CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD);
+
 #ifdef CONF_MP_INTR
 	if (cpu_interrupts_enabled(env)) {
 	    int	tt;
